      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### What the numbers mean\n\n- **CPU package** comes from RAPL (`node_rapl_package_joules_total`). The counter's rate is watts.\n- **GPU** comes from `node_hwmon_power_average_watt` (amdgpu) and `nvidia_smi_power_draw_watts` (NVIDIA).\n- This dashboard shows **silicon power**, not wall power. It excludes PSU/VRM losses, RAM, fans, NVMe, NIC, RGB and board overhead.\n- The UPS panel is the only true whole-rack number, but this UPS driver only reports **load percentage**, not real power, and it includes non-server devices too.\n\nTo see actual wall watts per machine, add a metered smart plug/PDU per host and export its power metric. Then this dashboard can add a true wall-power panel without changing the per-host workload metrics."
      },
      "title": "Metric sources and limitations",
      "type": "text"
    }
